## A06:2025 — Insecure Design

**Never generate**

- “Security by obscurity” as the only control; missing threat modeling for auth, payments, and data flows; rate limits omitted on auth and sensitive APIs by design.

**Always use instead**

- Design controls up front: threat assumptions, abuse cases, quotas, fraud limits, and safe defaults documented in code or ADRs where appropriate.
- Align architecture with trust boundaries (browser vs server vs third parties).

**Example**

```text
// Vulnerable: unlimited login attempts by design
POST /login — no throttle

// Secure: rate limit + lockout/backoff at design time
POST /login — per-IP and per-account throttling
```

